    "content": "CYTOGENETICS LABORATORY REPORT\n[redacted location] Medical Center\n\nPATIENT INFORMATION\nName: [redacted name]\nMRN: [redacted ID]\nDOB: [redacted date]\nAge/Sex: 51-year-old male\nOrdering Physician: Dr. [redacted name]\nDate Collected: [redacted date]\nDate Reported: [redacted date]\n\nCLINICAL DETAILS\nDiagnosis: Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL)\nReason for Referral: CLL patient requiring genetic analysis\n\nTEST PERFORMED\nInterphase Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) Analysis\n\nMETHODOLOGY\nInterphase FISH analysis was performed on peripheral blood specimens using the MultiGene CLL Panel. The following probes were utilized:\n- ATM (11q22.3) / CEP 11 dual color probe\n- DLEU (13q14) / 13qter dual color probe  \n- TP53 (17p13.1) / CEP 17 dual color probe\n- CEP 12 (chromosome 12 centromere) probe\n\nA total of 100 interphase nuclei were analyzed for each probe set according to standard laboratory protocols.\n\nRESULTS\n\nATM (11q22.3): No deletion detected\n- 100/100 cells with normal signal pattern (2R2G)\n- Normal cutoff: <6.5%\n\nDLEU (13q14): No deletion detected  \n- 100/100 cells with normal signal pattern (2R2G)\n- Normal cutoff: <7.5%\n\nTP53 (17p13.1): No deletion detected\n- 100/100 cells with normal signal pattern (2R2G)\n- Normal cutoff: <7.0%\n\nChromosome 12: Normal diploid complement\n- 100/100 cells with 2 centromeric signals\n- No evidence of trisomy 12\n\nINTERPRETATION\nInterphase FISH analysis reveals no deletion of ATM (11q22.3), DLEU (13q14), or TP53 (17p13.1) in the cells analyzed. A normal diploid complement of chromosome 12 centromeres was observed. These findings indicate no genetic abnormalities commonly associated with CLL were detected in this specimen.\n\nThe absence of these common CLL-associated cytogenetic abnormalities has favorable prognostic implications for this patient.\n\nReported by: [redacted name], PhD, FACMG\nLaboratory Director: [redacted name], MD",
